From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:26:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: clear the syscall-callback guard on the exec-request
 protect path

NtProtectVirtualMemory's [exec-req] diagnostic (the first 64 protects
that ask for execute) returned without leave_syscall_callback(), so the
thread's InSyscallCallback stayed set. Until something cleared it (FEX's
exception path does), enter_syscall_callback() refused on that thread
and every NtAllocate/NtProtect/NtFree/NtMapViewOfSection went to the raw
syscall with no FEX notification.

Code written into a PAGE_READWRITE allocation and then protected
PAGE_EXECUTE_READ was therefore never added to FEX's executable
intervals: the protect probe's exec-rw phase ended in
"[iOS-xquery] MISS", "NoExec instruction in entry block" and a read of
address 0. A PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE allocation worked only because its
allocation notification had come before the guard stuck.

Clear the guard on that path as on the normal one.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-noexec-rw-rx.md
Offered-upstream: no; the diagnostic exists only in the iOS port
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index 9d53a2f..ca8b951 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -2216,6 +2216,10 @@ NTSTATUS SYSCALL_API NtProtectVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *addr_ptr, SI
             else if (pNotifyMemoryProtect
                      && !ios_bulk_protect_suppressed( "cur-post", *addr_ptr, *size_ptr, new_prot ))
                 pNotifyMemoryProtect( *addr_ptr, *size_ptr, new_prot, TRUE, st );
+            /* This early return must clear the guard as the normal path does: left set,
+             * every later memory notification on the thread is dropped, and code made
+             * executable by a protect is never registered with FEX (NoExec). */
+            leave_syscall_callback();
             return st;
         }
     }
